Article 11
(1) Recovery Efforts as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (3) letter c, may be carried out, among others, through the following efforts:
a. Initial motivation from outreach results (raid operations);
b. Identification;
c. Selection;
d. Social motivation;
e. Placement/referral to rehabilitation institutions;
f. Return to the place of origin;
g. Social guidance and skills training;
h. Stimulus assistance;
i. Supervision.
(2) Handling of rehabilitative efforts may be carried out at institutions existing in the region and outside the region.
(3) In the implementation of rehabilitative efforts as referred to in paragraph (1), such efforts may be provided through guidance, education, training—physical, mental, and social—medical rehabilitation, job skills in accordance with their talents and abilities, social assistance, placement/referral, and further guidance.

